Well, let's see what I can remember, since I didn't take notes, and
I was too excited to remember to put my intrinsics, inventory etc. in a
text file... So no precise details.

Started out as a normal samurai, went straight to the mines after gaining
a couple of levels. Collected armor, found a longsword and started
two-weaponing it with my katana once I got the longsword-skill to expert.
Whacked monsters. Went to minetown, no magic lamps, no coaligned
altar. Hmmpff. Found stuff. Got the luckstone from mines end.
Dipped the longsword for Excalibur, took maybe 7 fountains to get it :)
#twoweaponed it with the katana, and never changed main weapons again.
(Had a +7 Excalibur and a +4 _very corroded_ katana when I ascended(!))

Back to the main dungeon branch. Sokoban contained an amulet of
reflection, that was nice. Went down a few levels again, found enough
cash (from vaults mostly) to get some protection.

Then to the Quest, after finding a nice tasty wraith when being clvl
13. No problems until the final level. My "oR saved me from
some samurai's wand of death, which I quickly made My wand of
death. Proceeded to Ashikaga Takauji with murder in my mind ;)
Zapped him, and missed, of course. I recall him getting four strikes in
with the Tsurugi (brrr...didn't have an "oLS) before I hit him with the
wand. Took the Bell and Tsurugi, and proceeded in the main branch. Found a
magic lamp lying around, and poof, suddenly had a +3 GDSM :) Threw away my
crappy +2 dwarvish mithril coat. By this point I probably had found a bag
of holding already, and was maybe clvl 15.

Raided Fort Ludios, and returned to a priest with huge amounts of
gold. Got a naked AC of 1, didn't really bother trying to get more
protection after donating the Ludios money.

The castle wand was at 3 charges.

Found nice pieces of armor and other stuff on the way down... Ended up
with speed boots, gauntlets of dex, cloak of displacement, polypiled
myself a T-shirt, found a spellbook of ID which helped quite a bit...
Probably wished the gauntlets or the boots, don't remember. But more
importantly, wished scrolls of genocide and a magic marker, wiped out some
of the more dangerous and/or annoying monsters like L,h,n,;,R,c. (Maybe
four of these at this point, and the rest later on) Oh yeah, and P, too,
when one tried to slime me... Wand of fire...*phew*

Gehennom. Juiblex made me sick, but I killed him the next turn, then used
an unihorn to heal myself. Then I just began digging down, since I had
found and/or wished enchant armor scrolls, and already had an AC of maybe
-30. Killed Asmodeus, Orcus, Baalzebub when coming back up from the
bottom :-)

This time I remembered to get the Candelabrum from Vlad before making
Rodney angry :-) Paid a visit to Izchak's shop before killing Rodney.
What? You think I would remember to buy those candles when I was there
before? ;-)

Rodney's tower didn't cause too much trouble. Rodney went down in four
doublestrikes, didn't want to waste my few wand of death charges.

Went down, had looked up the vibrating square in advance, did the
invocation. In Moloch's Sanctum my HP:s did even go to about 100 at one
point, even though I had an AC of -34. Probably because I had Double
Trouble Rodney and the high priest of Moloch whacking me...all at the same
time.

Killed them all. 

Took the amulet. Rodney appeared a couple of times, but the mysterious
force didn't throw me down levels even once, and I was lawful. Three or
four times to another location in the same level I tried to go up from,
but that was no big deal. Had tele and telecontrol, that speeded up the
process of running up through levels. Had also dug stair-to-stair
corridors.

Well done, mortal! But now thou must face the final Test...

"So thou thought thou couldst kill me, fool." Yes. I actually still think
so. Rodney ate my swords again.

At this point I realized I hadn't remembered to take/find enough gold
detection scrolls with me. Dug my bag. Had two. Luckily, I had remembered
to take a heap on confusion potions. Got through Earth quickly, with the
portal only maybe 15 squares away. Spent some time on air trying to find
the portal, no luck. The elementals aren't that bad, btw, at least
with an AC of -33 (Somebody smoldered my speed boots, as they weren't
fireproof). Used my other gold detection, jumped into the portal.

Then it struck me. I had about a dozen teleport and create monster scrolls
in my bag. HMM. Lemmesee... oh, a wand of polymorph! Nice!

Zap! No gold detection. Zap! TWO gold detection scrolls :-D

Levitated over lava with my Ring o' Lev, straight to the portal. In water
I was in no hurry, since I had genocided drowning monsters. Was there
until I stumbled into the final portal.

Astral. A tame angel of Amaterasu Omikami soon turned quite untame
as I put on my ring of conflict. Checked altars with telepathy, Pestilence
was straight up, Famine on the right. Straight up it is. Zap! Hit
Pestilence with the first shot with a wand of death. Ran around monsters
fighting each other, to find out that the altar was to
Raijin. Thought "Damn, of course my first ascension-maybe-to-be can't be
easy.". Pestilence rose from the dead, but was busy whacking angels when I
ran past. Went to see Famine... Famine saw the wrong end of a wand of
death. And the altar is... to Susanowo. "GODDAMMIT!". No helm of opposite
alignment in my bag. Was going to the final altar, got maybe six squares
from Susanowo's altar, when a player-monster blocked my way. Whacked her
(a valkyrie) down. Luckily I checked what she dropped. A Helm Of Opposite
Alignment!!! :D :D :D Took it, went those few squares back to the altar of
Susanowo, changed my helmet, offered the Amulet. I love the RNG for giving
me that HoOA :-)

"In return for thy service, I grant thee the gift of Immortality!"

Feel free to any questions, and I'll try to remember. Now there are
clearly large gaps in this story.

Now I'll go sit in a corner and be pleased with myself ;-)

